description:
Elements without their own focus style (e.g. article rows, frontend/src/components/article/article-item.tsx, a div tabIndex=0) get the browser's default focus outline. Chrome shows it after any keyboard press (j/k shortcuts, Esc closing a dialog), so it pops up on a clicked row while the selection is elsewhere, half-clipped by the scroll area.
User decision 2026-10-10: remove only that default; the styled focus-visible:ring-*/outline-* utilities in components/ui stay.
Change: new file frontend/src/no-default-outline.css, imported with one line at the end of the @import block in frontend/src/index.css, containing
  @layer base { :focus-visible { outline-style: none; } }
In the base layer so Tailwind utilities (utilities layer) still win where a component styles its own outline. One comment line: why.
May change: those two files only. Do not edit components/ui/*.
